<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Corpus Sources — the registry that DERIVES

A corpus is a read-only top-level bag, one Automerge doc per corpus, composed into any room or view by
the recipe layer.

''The registry is not a table any more.'' A vessel discovers its corpora by walking the CATALOG plane
for entries under `CATALOG_CORPUS_PREFIX` — each entry's title carries the corpus id and its text
carries the doc url — and derives the bag URI from the id with `corpusLarUri(slug)`. Nothing enumerates
them ahead of time, so a corpus added to the catalog is a corpus the next boot loads, with no constant
to edit and none to go stale.

''This room held that enumeration, and the enumeration rotted while the derivation ran'' — three of its
seven listed paths no longer exist, and it counted five. The derive-don't-enumerate law, learned on this
carrier's own body.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Law

A corpus source MUST carry:

```toml
name  — pnpm workspace package name (@lararium/corpus-<slug>)
path  — relative path from monorepo root
bag   — Automerge bag name (matches LarTiddlerRecord["bag"])
```

The loader discovers carrier files by walking the corpus path at hydration time.
It produces `LarTiddlerRecord[]` via the projection codec — one record per tiddler.
Carrier text does not travel to Automerge directly.

The quine-corpus (`lares`) differs: it also defines the infrastructure the machinery reads.
It hydrates before all other corpora. All other corpora treat it as read-only at runtime.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/registry>>

!! Where a corpus comes from

# ''The catalog names it.'' A `corpus:` entry lives in the catalog plane at
`lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/catalog/corpus/<slug>`, its text the corpus doc's AutomergeUrl. The catalog
CATALOGS; it does not host.
# ''The id derives the bag.'' `corpusLarUri(slug)` reads `lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/<slug>`. Every corpus is
a first-class bag at child[1] under the bag-tag rule.
# ''The entry MAY declare a scale.'' An entry carrying a mesh scale federates through the tideline
resolver; an undeclared entry mints local. A peer still joining SKIPS its layer and reconciles later —
never a blank ghost standing in for content that has not arrived.
# ''The loader is ONE body for both vessels.'' `loadCatalogCorpora` adds each entry as a read-only layer
on the composite; node and browser differ only in an injected local-mint factory and a provenance string.

''The `lares` corpus differs'': it defines the infrastructure the machinery itself reads, so it hydrates
before the others, which treat it as read-only at runtime.

''Carrier text never travels to Automerge directly.'' The loader walks a corpus's carriers at hydration
and produces `LarTiddlerRecord[]` through the projection codec — one record per tiddler.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bag-recipe-topology>>

!! Bag/Recipe Topology

```
system bag    ← invariant TW5 boot corpus (read-only)
lararium bag  ← engine self-doc memes for the TypeScript packages
lares bag     ← infrastructure-as-myth; the QUINE corpus, read at runtime by the machinery itself
elyncia bag   ← setting content
sdm bag       ← SDM core rules
crossroads    ← the announce plane
room bag      ← situated meaning: pins, notes, active artifacts
draft bag     ← local high-churn drafts (not synced to peers)
projection    ← rebuildable shadow; receipt-tagged
```

A recipe composes any subset of these bags for a given view.
SDM+ as a combined view composes: lares + elyncia + sdm + room.
A setting-only table composes: lares + elyncia + room.

<<~/ahu>>

